Original customer complaint (relayed by a risk control specialist at a certain bank, {date} {time}):
"On what grounds are you throttling my account? All 3 posts I published on {date} were suppressed to 0 views. My account has been registered for 5 years, and I have never received a single violation notice. Please give me an explanation immediately, or I will go to the complaint platform."
— Ticket {ticket}, source {site}

Verification record:
1. The account has no violation records in the past 180 days, a credit score of 100, and 0 historical appeals;
2. The 3 posts were manually reviewed and are all original life records; they do not involve traffic diversion, sensitive topics, or minors appearing on camera;
3. The real reason the views dropped to zero is a 3-hour 20-minute delay in third-party data return, which caused the {batch} batch data not to be written to the database. This is the same batch issue as the delay in {ticket} on the previous day, and the data has now been backfilled;
4. The other 2 accounts under the same device {device} have normal data, so device-level risk control can be ruled out.
Itemized scores: violation 0 points + content risk 0 points + device risk 1 point (the device had one off-site login within 30 days, and it has been confirmed in person that it was the user) = weighted cumulative 1 point; according to the grading table, 0-2 points is Low (tier 0). The handling standard for this tier is no restriction, only replying to the appeal and apologizing.
Note: The complainant also asked how to issue an invoice for {order_no}; forwarded to finance, unrelated to the determination of this ticket.
